    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17443653_3651cf7b",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-16T05:33:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we move the old data? Can\u0027t we just use a circular buffer instead? (using erased space as end/start indicators).",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "320f0b6e_9c98c335",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-17T20:03:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think moving data simplifies log management, also, note that you need to erase the entire page anyways, so a portion of the log needs to be re-written in any case.",
      "parentUuid": "17443653_3651cf7b",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21805416_267e0663",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-21T04:15:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, it was my first reaction as well (the benefit is we can retain more unread entries when we reach the full log: 100% of its size instead of 25%). but if we do circular buffer, we\u0027ll have to erase \u0026 rewrite the log page in flash on every addition of the new log entry, instead of doing erase only when we are compacting. which may not be great for flash wear - not sure if that\u0027s a concern.",
      "parentUuid": "320f0b6e_9c98c335",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5c73a10_431ed465",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-21T14:36:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "both wear and time - writing a few bytes of the new record is much faster than erasing the page and rewriting it.\n\nThe main idea of this is that the log grows very slow and is polled by the host often, so there is no harm in dropping old entries.",
      "parentUuid": "21805416_267e0663",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "831d5b04_1a2570ab",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T03:14:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e we\u0027ll have to erase \u0026 rewrite the log page in flash on every addition of the new log entry,\n\nReally? Normally you can just keep writing to an erased page.",
      "parentUuid": "f5c73a10_431ed465",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "858a199b_befe9cf1",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T04:26:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "here are two options:\n\n- we try keeping a full circular log. We start with an empty page, then the log fills up and we need to wrap around. At this point if we want to keep the entire log, we\u0027d need to erase the entire page, write back most of the log and just overwrite  a little part of it, large enough for the new entry.\n\nThis is not a good idea for a couple obvious reasons:\n   . erasing the page every time is really expensive from flash wear \n     standpoint\n   . erasing and rewriting the entire page will take long time\n\n- we do not try to keep a full log. We keep filling it up until it is close to capacity, and then preserve the last 25% of it, erase the page and write the 25% of contents back. Erasing would happen much less often now, not with every new entry, but only when log is close to capacity. Saving new entries would be much faster, as there is no erase involved and just a few bytes have to be written, not 2K.\n\nSo, we need to write back the preserved 25% of the log - why not to write them at the beginning - in this case there is no need to worry about wrapping.\n\n\nDoes this make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "831d5b04_1a2570ab",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65017862_f6efcfac",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T05:43:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. I think what I had in mind is log size \u003e erase size (page). If log size \u003d\u003d erase size, then there is no point using a circular log.",
      "parentUuid": "858a199b_befe9cf1",
      "revId": "3929f4f23875c7fd3eb7bdb434dafcdde9a34480",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
